<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="bar">
    <a class="home" href="https://charlietrenorden.com/"><span class="back">&larr;</span>Other projects</a>
    <button class="toggle" id="themeBtn" type="button" aria-label="Toggle light and dark theme"><span class="dot"></span><span id="themeLbl">Dark</span></button>
  </div>

  <h1>Position Record</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every position I hold, the reasoning as it stood when I opened it, and the record before it.</p>   <!-- PAIRED with meta description, word for word. -->

  <h2>Open</h2>
{% for p in rows %}
  <div class="pos">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="nm">{{ p.name }}</span>
      <span class="dir {{ p.direction | lower }}">{{ p.direction }}</span>
      <span class="kind">{{ p.kind }} &middot; opened {{ p.entry_date }}</span>
      <span class="r {{ 'up' if p.r >= 0 else 'dn' }}">{{ '%+.2f'|format(p.r) }}R</span>
    </div>
    <ul class="why">
{% for line in p.thesis %}      <li>{{ line }}</li>
{% endfor %}    </ul>
    <div class="figs">
      <span><b>Entry</b>{{ p.entry | px(p.dp) }}</span>
      <span><b>Stop</b>{{ p.stop | px(p.dp) }}</span>
      <span><b>Target</b>{{ p.target | px(p.dp) }} <span style="color:var(--faint)">({{ '%.1f'|format(p.reward_r) }}R)</span></span>
      <span><b>Last</b>{{ p.price | px(p.dp) }}</span>
      <span class="carry {{ 'rx' if p.carry_dir == 'received' else 'px' }}"><b>Carry</b>{{ '%+.2f'|format(p.carry_pct) }}%/yr {{ p.carry_dir }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="gauge">
      <div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: {{ '%.0f'|format(p.stop_left * 100 if p.stop_left < 1 else 100) }}%"></div></div>
      <span class="cap">{{ '%.2f'|format(p.stop_left) }}R left to the stop</span>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endfor %}

  <h2>Closed</h2>
{% if closed %}
{% for c in closed %}
  <div class="pos">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="nm">{{ c.name }}</span>
      <span class="dir {{ c.direction | lower }}">{{ c.direction }}</span>
      <span class="kind">{{ c.entry_date }} to {{ c.exit_date }}</span>
      <span class="r {{ 'up' if c.r >= 0 else 'dn' }}">{{ '%+.2f'|format(c.r) }}R</span>
    </div>
    <ul class="why">
{% for line in c.thesis %}      <li>{{ line }}</li>
{% endfor %}      <li><b>Outcome.</b> {{ c.outcome }}</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
  <p class="empty">Nothing closed yet under this page's rules.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if hist %}
  <h2>Before this page</h2>

  <p class="say">I traded this account for fourteen months before I started writing the
  reasoning down. It lost {{ '%.0f'|format(-hist.net_pnl_pct) }}% of what I put into it.
  Here is where the money went, because the answer is not the one I expected.</p>

  <dl class="ledger">
    <dt>Paid in, {{ hist.paid_in_count }} deposits</dt><dd>{{ hist.paid_in | aud }}</dd>
    <dt>Taken back out</dt><dd>{{ hist.taken_out | aud }}</dd>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <dt class="big">Net in</dt><dd class="big">{{ hist.net_in | aud }}</dd>
    <dt>Balance today</dt><dd>{{ hist.balance | aud }}</dd>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <dt class="big">Result</dt><dd class="big dn">{{ hist.net_pnl | aud }}</dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="say">{{ hist.cost_share_of_loss }}% of that loss never went to the market. It
  went to the broker.</p>

  <dl class="ledger">
    <dt>Commission, {{ hist.costs.commission_charges }} charges</dt><dd class="hit">{{ hist.costs.commission | aud }}</dd>
    <dt>Holding costs, {{ hist.costs.holding_charges }} daily charges</dt><dd>{{ hist.costs.holding | aud }}</dd>
    <dt>Market data</dt><dd>{{ hist.costs.market_data | aud }}</dd>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <dt class="big">Total cost</dt><dd class="big hit">{{ hist.costs.total | aud }}</dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="say">Every dollar of that commission was on share CFDs. CMC charges none on
  currencies, indices or commodities, so the split is not close: {{ (-hist.costs.commission_on_share_cfds) | aud }}
  against {{ (-hist.costs.commission_on_macro) | aud }}. My median hold over that
  period was {{ hist.median_hold_days }} days, so I was paying around
  {{ (2 * -hist.costs.commission / hist.costs.commission_charges) | aud }} in commission
  to hold a share for {{ hist.median_hold_days }} days in an account this size. No edge survives that, and it is not a question of whether the trades were any
  good. Everything I hold now is priced by spread and financing instead, which is why
  the carry number sits on every position above.</p>

  <p class="say">The {{ hist.trades|length }} trades below are what I could pair from the
  statements between {{ hist.first_row }} and {{ hist.last_row }}. {{ hist.win_pct }}%
  of them made money. They do not add up to the result at the top: they miss positions
  that opened or closed outside the statement windows, and they exclude every cost in
  the table above. The account figure is what actually happened. This is a partial view
  of how.</p>

  <div class="scroller">
  <table class="rec">
    <thead><tr>
      <th>Closed</th><th>Product</th><th>Dir</th>
      <th class="n">Hold</th><th class="n">Move</th><th class="n">R</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
{% for t in hist.trades %}      <tr>
        <td>{{ t.exit_date }}</td>
        <td class="p">{{ t.product }}</td>
        <td>{{ t.direction }}</td>
        <td class="n">{{ t.hold_days }}d</td>
        <td class="n {{ 'up' if t.move_pct > 0 else 'dn' }}">{{ '%+.2f'|format(t.move_pct) }}%</td>
{% if t.r is not none %}        <td class="n {{ 'up' if t.r > 0 else 'dn' }}">{{ '%+.2f'|format(t.r) }}</td>
{% else %}        <td class="n na">no stop</td>
{% endif %}      </tr>
{% endfor %}    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note">R is blank on {{ hist.trades|length - hist.with_r }} of these because no
  stop was recorded when the position opened, and a stop set later is a trailing stop
  rather than the risk I had accepted. Across the {{ hist.with_r }} that do carry one the
  mean is {{ '%+.2f'|format(hist.mean_r) }}R. The account reached {{ hist.peak_balance | aud }}
  on {{ hist.peak_date }} and hit zero on {{ hist.zeroed|join(' and ') }}.</p>
{% endif %}

  <p class="note"><b>1R</b> is the distance from the entry to the stop I set when I opened
  the position, so it is the loss I had accepted before I knew the answer. Everything here
  is quoted in multiples of it, which makes a peso position and an index position
  comparable and means the page discloses no position sizes. Prices are the market mid
  as at {{ asof }}, not my broker's fill. Not investment advice.</p>
</div>

<script>
  var root = document.documentElement;
  var btn = document.getElementById("themeBtn"), lbl = document.getElementById("themeLbl");
  function sync() { lbl.textContent = root.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark" ? "Dark" : "Light"; }
  sync();
  btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
    var dark = root.getAttribute("data-theme") !== "dark";
    root.setAttribute("data-theme", dark ? "dark" : "light");
    try { localStorage.setItem("theme", dark ? "dark" : "light"); } catch (e) {}
    sync();
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
